// Fellowship :: version 0.1.0
// Released May 27th, 2005
// Changelog

5.27.2k5	First release 0.1.0

2026-10-20	(AIDA) Discourse referents: "theorem x : [?r1:S1, ..., ?rn] P"
		holds the referents ?r in the goal's environment, infers
		their sorts, and refuses "qed" on such a theorem.
2026-10-22	(AIDA) A referent may also be written !r.
2026-10-26	(AIDA) Instantiating a quantifier no longer captures: the
		substitution stops at a binder of the substituted name and,
		where it substitutes, renames a binder of a name in the
		substituted term (y to y2, y3, ..., as AIDA does).  0.1.0 accepted false theorems.

